# Project development (local)

You are helping **maintain the agentic-design-system starter pack itself**.

This is different from helping someone *use* the starter to build their design system.

## Local files (gitignored — not shipped)

1. Read [`.cursor/AGENTS.dev.md`](../AGENTS.dev.md) for maintainer agent guidance.
2. Read [`.cursor/plans/PLAN.md`](../plans/PLAN.md) for roadmap, phases, and the simplicity rule.
3. Do not copy maintainer roadmap or tooling war stories into published `docs/` or root `AGENTS.md`.

## Simplicity (tooling)

Prefer the smallest solution that works for `npm run storybook` / `npm run tokens:build`. Do not add Node path helpers, markdown plugins, cache scripts, or `@types/*` “just in case.”

Details: `.cursor/plans/PLAN.md` and `.cursor/AGENTS.dev.md`.

## Separation rule

| Audience | Where guidance lives |
|----------|----------------------|
| Teams building *their* design system | `AGENTS.md`, `docs/`, other `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` |
| Maintainers of *this* starter repo | `.cursor/AGENTS.dev.md`, `.cursor/plans/PLAN.md`, this rule |

When unclear, prefer the published design-system guides and ask before adding maintainer notes to synced files.
